      "id": "s4",
      "concept": "Net Force Vector",
      "narration": "The net force is the vector sum of all forces acting on an object. It determines acceleration, not just magnitude, because direction matters. For example, if two forces push at right angles, the net force is found using the Pythagorean theorem.",
